# Optional. Nothing in compose.yaml needs a `.env` any more: every password
# and key is generated into the formancy-data-secrets volume on the first
# start and read from there (see compose.yaml's header for how to read one).
#
# What may be set here, or in the environment, is where compose publishes on
# loopback, for a machine where the default port is already taken. Copy to
# `.env` and uncomment a line to use it; `.env` is gitignored.

# The web front: the studio at /studio/, the host page at /host/, /v1 behind
# them. Started by `--profile stack` only.
# FORMANCY_DATA_WEB_PORT=4394

# PostgreSQL.
# FORMANCY_DATA_PG_PORT=5440

# SQL Server.
# FORMANCY_DATA_MS_PORT=1434
